{"lines":[{"t":"1718867188","x":0.7716049391467531,"w":0.069958845774332645,"y":0.046511627815394085,"h":0.008720930389296444,"c":0.5},{"c":1,"t":"Test 3","x":0.1172839502042468,"y":0.053779069625663367,"w":0.057613169352213542,"h":0.013081395583944611},{"t":"One response to the boycott movement has been the argument for the vital role palm","y":0.097383721119014943,"c":1,"w":0.67078186035156251,"x":0.16255145699842993,"h":0.014534882858869391},{"x":0.15843621828536006,"y":0.11482558126253128,"t":"oil plays in lifting many millions of people in the developing world out of poverty. Is it","w":0.69341562906901044,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"t":"desirable to have palm oil boycotted, replaced, eliminated from the global supply chain,","h":0.017773886591862964,"c":1,"y":0.13050912539207282,"w":0.69768269856770848,"x":0.16041860762994314},{"y":0.14811542992807047,"x":0.16049383709555939,"t":"given how many low-income people in developing countries depend on it for their","w":0.65637858072916666,"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"livelihoods? How best to strike a utilitarian balance between these competing factors has","x":0.16049383774655535,"y":0.16424418591279055,"w":0.70781890869140629,"h":0.014534883982160851},{"w":0.30041152954101563,"h":0.011629619081674702,"c":1,"y":0.18168433450678512,"t":"become a serious bone of contention.","x":0.160493823594625},{"h":0.011627907185728703,"y":0.21366279047690306,"x":0.11728395063799979,"c":1,"t":"F","w":0.012345678806304938},{"t":"Even the deforestation argument isn't as straightforward as it seems. Oil palm plantations","x":0.16049383680173701,"y":0.21366279055120241,"c":1,"w":0.71399175008138016,"h":0.016019188192342826},{"x":0.16049382328864822,"y":0.23110465102976896,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.69135803222656245,"t":"produce at least four and potentially up to ten times more oil per hectare than soybean,"},{"y":0.24705535913253518,"c":1,"x":0.15843621539949082,"w":0.66049382527669276,"h":0.016026036337772775,"t":"rapeseed, sunflower or other competing oils. That immensely high yield - which is"},{"y":0.26442873986130722,"t":"predominantly what makes it so profitable - is potentially also an ecological benefit. If ten","x":0.16049382768554685,"w":0.71810699462890626,"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1},{"y":0.28052325568046577,"t":"times more palm oil can be produced from a patch of land than any competing oil, then ten","h":0.014534883982160629,"w":0.72427983601888013,"c":1,"x":0.16049382676275856},{"c":1,"y":0.29507543965161409,"t":"times more land would need to be cleared in order to produce the same volume of oil from","w":0.72240020751953127,"x":0.15835412718659483,"h":0.018655607360552273},{"x":0.15811629639151306,"t":"that competitor.","y":0.31337452532090504,"h":0.016403771682397705,"c":1,"w":0.13024611155192059},{"c":1,"w":0.72647242228190101,"t":"As for the question of carbon emissions, the issue really depends on what oil palm trees are","x":0.1624733039596607,"y":0.34555365001322957,"h":0.017541776416720167},{"t":"replacing. Crops vary in the degree to which they sequester carbon - in other words, the","x":0.15843620821840279,"y":0.36336866908446341,"w":0.70370371500651041,"h":0.015991796172268979,"c":1},{"y":0.39540307793620011,"c":1,"x":0.16042619671342076,"t":"carbon a plant sequesters, the more it reduces the effect of climate change. As Shankar","w":0.6914995320638021,"h":0.016714849797800357},{"c":1,"x":0.15843620632316904,"t":"explains: '[Palm oil production] actually sequesters more carbon in some ways than other","w":0.71604939778645826,"y":0.41279069752735442,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"y":0.42873969357056851,"w":0.71810699462890637,"c":1,"h":0.016027747672073156,"x":0.15843621155900364,"t":"alternatives. [...] Of course, if you're cutting down virgin forest it's terrible - that's what's"},{"y":0.44611307446366366,"t":"happening in Indonesia and Malaysia, it's been allowed to get out of hand. But if it's","x":0.15843621294472371,"w":0.67283950805664072,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"y":0.46220930216500133,"c":1,"w":0.55349792480468751,"t":"replacing rice, for example, it might actually sequester more carbon?","h":0.017472676590558844,"x":0.15843622269899593},{"w":0.70576131184895852,"c":1,"t":"The industry is now regulated by a group called the Roundtable on Sustainable Palm Oil","x":0.16049382957380723,"h":0.016044868316470673,"y":0.49558303880147536},{"h":0.018918961883293339,"c":1,"w":0.72235448201497399,"t":"(RSPO), consisting of palm growers, retailers, product manufacturers, and other interested","x":0.15837600687834916,"y":0.5114432787935822},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.15843620918640872,"w":0.69753087361653643,"t":"parties. Over the past decade or so, an agreement has gradually been reached regarding","y":0.5290697672954553,"c":1},{"t":"standards that producers of palm oil have to meet in order for their product to be regarded","y":0.54505300370010579,"w":0.71810699462890615,"h":0.015993508068214979,"c":1,"x":0.15843621455965462},{"y":0.560954063860852,"h":0.017667844522968212,"x":0.1584362164386213,"t":"as officially 'sustainable'. The RSPO insists upon no virgin forest clearing, transparency and","w":0.73868311564127609,"c":1},{"t":"fully satisfied is the oil allowed to be sold as certified sustainable palm oil (CSPO). Recent","x":0.15843621356080112,"y":0.5959302324251492,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.72427983601888024,"c":1},{"t":"figures show that the RSPO now certifies around 12 million tonnes of palm oil annually,","y":0.61072943847134453,"x":0.16045038198402342,"w":0.70380813598632819,"h":0.017199547748543154,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.62926972886772847,"x":0.15843621797551766,"t":"equivalent to roughly 21 percent of the world's total palm oil production.","w":0.58436213175455731,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"h":0.017376408279293099,"t":"There is even hope that oil palm plantations might not need to be such sterile monocultures,","c":1,"w":0.73880742390950527,"y":0.65996927269614525,"x":0.15632335091846566},{"h":0.016046579650771164,"w":0.70781890869140629,"y":0.67726737321977737,"c":1,"x":0.1625514454485357,"t":"or 'green deserts', as Ellwood describes them. New research at Ellwood's lab hints at one"},{"y":0.69611307447681658,"w":0.72839508056640634,"t":"plant which might make all the difference. The bird's nest fern (Asplenium nidus) grows on","c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.15843620445479417},{"x":0.15843620731146832,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"trees in an epiphytic fashion (meaning it's dependent on the tree only for support, not for","y":0.71220930219241629},{"x":0.16255143998789567,"t":"nutrients), and is native to many tropical regions, where as a keystone species it performs a","w":0.72427983601888024,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"y":0.72819767428378857},{"t":"vital ecological role. Ellwood believes that reintroducing the bird's nest fern into oil palm","w":0.71399175008138016,"c":1,"y":0.74558303881484256,"x":0.15843622362124715,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"plantations could potentially allow these areas to recover their biodiversity, providing a","y":0.76148409914616666,"x":0.15843622645003791,"w":0.69547322591145844,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"w":0.70781890869140629,"t":"home for all manner of species, from fungi and bacteria, to invertebrates such as insects,","h":0.014534883982160851,"x":0.1604938375183832,"y":0.77761627893260488,"c":1},{"t":"amphibians, reptiles and even mammals.","x":0.16049382345467203,"y":0.79505300371100684,"c":1,"h":0.01454001966999896,"w":0.32921811421712244},{"w":0.026748971939086916,"c":1,"y":0.86773255795657411,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"64","x":0.11522633698313144},{"y":0.95314993796778535,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30612678527832038,"c":1,"h":0.03375352650564889,"x":0.66991655033568553}],"h":3395,"w":2400}